# The editor's top bar
// Joined to the top of the window, with three sections:
// Spell's menu, the project's menu and the app's menus, then Run and Edit in the middle, then the tools and you.
// What's in each is still the editor's own, `EditorToolbar` in `SpellEditor.tsx`:  each is a thing here that draws itself.

editor bar is an app:
	// Spell's menu:  its hat and name, opening the group's projects and Home
	its "spell menu" is a thing
	// The project's menu:  its name
	its "project menu" is a thing
	// File, Edit, View, Run and Help
	its "app menus" is a thing
	// Run and Edit, then Inspect app and the code's icon in Edit
	its "mode buttons" is a thing
	// Add and the Inspector's menu in Edit, then Restart and the theme
	its "tools" is a thing
	// The person's own menu
	its "you" is a thing

	to draw it:
		<ui-menu appearance="header" class="AppMenu tight EditorBar">
			<ui-menu position="left" class="third side">
				{draw its spell menu}
				{draw its project menu}
				{draw its app menus}
				<ui-item class="spring no-border"/>
			</ui-menu>
			<ui-menu position="left" class="third">
				<ui-item class="spring no-border"/>
				{draw its mode buttons}
				<ui-item class="spring no-border"/>
			</ui-menu>
			<ui-menu position="right" class="third side BarTools">
				<ui-item class="spring no-border"/>
				<ui-menu appearance="capsule">
					{draw its tools}
				</ui-menu>
				{draw its you}
			</ui-menu>
		</ui-menu>
